From: mix2-port <mix2@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: snoc: limit DMA to 32 bits on MSM8998

On MSM8998 (Xiaomi Mi MIX 2, WLAN.HL.1.0 firmware) WMI works but no
frame is ever received: scans hop channels without finding any BSS and
the modem watchdog then fires (DOG_HB starvation) while the WLAN process
waits on its RX path. The stock kernel confines all WLAN DMA to a
32-bit IOVA window (0xa0000000-0xb0000000), whereas with the 35-bit mask
the IOMMU hands out addresses like 0x7fe106140 that this generation of
the WLAN DMA cannot reach. Use a 32-bit mask on MSM8998.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c
@@ -1727,7 +1727,12 @@ static int ath10k_snoc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, drv_data->dma_mask);
+	/* The MSM8998 WLAN DMA only reaches 32-bit IOVAs */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,msm8998"))
+		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	else
+		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, drv_data->dma_mask);
+
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to set dma mask: %d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
